      en: ["Atlántida is located 45 kilometers east of Montevideo.", "It was founded in 1911 by a group of doctors.", "The Cristo Obrero church by Eladio Dieste is an architectural landmark.", "The city's name was suggested by writer Florencio Sánchez.", "The population was 5,562 inhabitants according to the 2011 census.", "It is the main resort of the Costa de Oro.", "Atlántida was elevated to city status on September 7, 1967, by Law No. 13.609.", "A famous building is 'El Águila', a mysterious stone construction."],
      es: ["Atlántida ofrece una visión profunda de la cultura y la tradición regionales.", "La ciudad se caracteriza por su diversidad arquitectónica e importancia histórica.", "Los viajeros encuentran en los alrededores de Atlántida diversas opciones para el ocio activo."],
      pt: ["Atlántida oferece uma visão profunda da cultura e tradição regionais.", "A cidade caracteriza-se pela sua diversidade arquitetónica e importância histórica.", "Os viajantes encontram nos arredores de Atlántida diversas opções para o lazer ativo."],
      fr: ["Atlántida offre un aperçu profond de la culture et des traditions régionales.", "La ville se caractérise par sa diversité architecturale et son importance historique.", "Les voyageurs trouveront dans les environs d'Atlántida de nombreuses possibilités de loisirs actifs."],
